          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}M(5)&=\\frac{180}{5}=36\\\\M(15)&=\\frac{180}{15}=12\\\\M(30)&=\\frac{180}{30}=6\\end{aligned}$\n\nEnter 36, 12 and 6 in the table. Plot $(5,36)$, $(15,12)$ and $(30,6)$, then join them with a smooth decreasing reciprocal curve for $5\\leq T\\leq30$.",
